  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup white sugar",
    "1 cup soy sauce",
    "1 cup water",
    "0.25 cup minced garlic",
    "0.25 cup minced fresh ginger",
    "5 pounds bone-in chicken thighs with skin",
    "0.25 cup chopped green onions"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather the ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/G4IjoKFi6wtB0U3niSi1tzd7Oj8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/222712-soy-sauce-chicken-ddmfs-3388-4x3-step-01-dde650152feb4871933909db03e56b1b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/222712/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine sugar, soy sauce, water, garlic, and ginger into a large stockpot over medium heat; stir until sugar dissolves.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GocBhlg0smHHrtuwBjnY4eVo3Rs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/222712-soy-sauce-chicken-ddmfs-3392-4x3-step-02-07fb2587ff424fc48e1603a4f590258e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/222712/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add chicken thighs and bring to a boil. Simmer, turning the chicken thighs with tongs every 5 minutes, until the sauce is a rich, brown glaze and the chicken is no longer pink at the bone and juices run clear, about 35 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted near the bone should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Remove pot from the heat and let cool 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/yTTf5fmjUjd453rholtA4ZePdLE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/222712-soy-sauce-chicken-ddmfs-3402-4x3-step-03-dd190f26dee8437292f5b6bbcb43272d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/222712/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer chicken thighs to a platter; sprinkle with chopped green onions.",
